seductive:
Oh the night is sweet for sleeping, but the shining day’s for working;
Sons of the seductive night, for your children’s children’s sake,
From the deep primeval forests where the crouching leopard’s lurking,

sedge:
For ever the same;
A drift of sedge;
A white, white stone;

sedate:
Estranged by consciousness from sentiment,
With a thought feeling forced to be sedate
Even when the feeling’s nature is violent;

seduction:
Upon this sleeping child,—man’s violence,
Not man’s seduction, made me what I am,
As lost as ... I told him I should be lost;
